  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-rc.2\n\n\t\tFramework alignment release. No changes to this package's own surface: the WASM orchestrator, the hub client and the widget behave exactly as in 1.0.0-rc.1, and the wire protocol is unchanged.\n\n\t\t=== Why the version moved ==================================================\n\t\t- The family moves onto the Agent Framework 1.18.0 line so the core package can adopt AgentSkillsSource and the ToolApprovalAgent middleware. All five packages ship together and share one version.\n\n\t\t=== Verified again on the new line ========================================\n\t\t- A cross-origin turn over SignalR against MentorAgent.Server: connected, streamed and completed in 14.4 s with a rendered table and RAG citation chips.\n\t\t- The double script tag - the configuration the documentation recommends here, where index.html carries a versioned tag and the widget injects a second - still leaves the voice state machine intact. That was BUG-039 in rc.1 and the fix holds.\n\n\t\t=== A sample-configuration trap worth knowing ==============================\n\t\t- Cross-origin failures surface in the browser as \"TypeError: Failed to fetch\", which reads exactly like a library defect and usually is not one. In our own sample the cause was two files disagreeing: the client was started on one port while the server's CORS list allowed another. Check the server's WithOrigins list against the port your client actually runs on before looking anywhere else.",
